PF1-PF18, PF19 ... are F1-F19, F19 ... Use shift for the next set of PF's after 9 but chances are, the defaults are the same
Page up and Page down work as instructed for PF8 and PF9
Using the numpad is great but not as expected. Num-1 goes to the end of the record, 7 goes back to command bar, tab to next input
Stacking commands can be done by adding a ';' between commands. for example, start;3.4; <== This starts a new screen, then uses the input '3.4' which goes to search
PF3 to go back a page, 
PF4 to go back a bunch,
PF5 to repeat a command, such as a find command in a cobol program.
